025-12-12T23:00:16Z","git_url":"git://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:bazelbuild/bazel.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel","homepage":"https://bazel.build","size":992874,"stargazers_count":24886,"watchers_count":24886,"language":"Java","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":4359,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1818,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["bazel","build","build-system","correct","fast","multi-language","scalable","test"],"visibility":"public","forks":4359,"open_issues":1818,"watchers":24886,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Description of the problem / feature request:\r\n\r\nThe `http_archive` [documentation](https://docs.bazel.build/versions/master/be/workspace.html#http_archive) refers to the new Skylark rule as being a drop-in replacement. The replacement is not drop-in, though, as the referenced build file (used when transitioning from the deprecated `new_http_archive` to the Skylark `http_archive`) is anticipated to live in an `external` folder. Calling the new Skylark rule a drop-in replacement without mentioning the requirement on a referenced build file is confusing.\r\n\r\n### Feature requests: what underlying problem are you trying to solve with this feature?\r\n\r\nAttempting to solve confusion when transitioning from older Bazel versions to newer versions.\r\n\r\n### Bugs: what's the simplest, easiest way to reproduce this bug? Please provide a minimal example if possible.\r\n\r\nSee issue [5890](https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/5890).\r\n\r\n### What operating system are you running Bazel on?\r\n\r\nUbuntu 18.04.\r\n\r\n### What's the output of `bazel info release`?\r\n\r\n```\r\nINFO: Invocation ID: 803d2a83-d8fb-4357-a52d-c8f313aa8cd5\r\nrelease 0.20.0\r\n```\r\n\r\n### If `bazel info release` returns \"development version\" or \"(@non-git)\", tell us how you built Bazel.\r\n\r\nN/A\r\n\r\n### What's the output of `git remote get-url origin ; git rev-parse master ; git rev-parse HEAD` ?\r\n\r\nN/A\r\n\r\n###  Have you found anything relevant by searching the web?\r\n\r\nI found issue [5890](https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/5890) coincidentally by searching for \"Not a regular file.\"\r\n\r\n### Any other information, logs, or outputs that you want to share?\r\n\r\nN/A","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/6873/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/6873/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":2189692580,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDIxODk2OTI1ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/events/2189692580","actor":{"login":"dslomov","id":5008223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMDgyMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5008223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov","html_url":"https://github.com/dslomov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dslomov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d